  "question": {
    "text": "For a concave lens of focal length <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi></math>, the relation between object and image distance <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>u</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo></math> respectively, from its pole can best be represented by (<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>u</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>v</mi></math> is the reference line):"
  },
  "options": [
